WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:04.760
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍尔。

2
00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:06.060
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金赛。

3
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:07.340
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演《办公室》。

4
00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:08.600
And we're best friends.
我们还是最好的朋友。

5
00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:12.420
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.
现在，我们专为你制作了这档《办公室》终极重温播客。

6
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:19.400
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.
每周，我们都会剖析一集《办公室》，并分享只有身临其境的我们两人才能告诉你的独家幕后故事。

7
00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:20.540
We're The Office ladies.
我们是《办公室》女士。

8
00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:28.500
All right, we are sitting across from each other, you guys.
好了，各位，我们现在正面对面坐着呢。

9
00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:33.360
This is very exciting because 2022, we couldn't do this until now.
这太令人兴奋了，因为在2022年，我们直到现在才能做到这一点。

10
00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:35.960
Until now, I'm tearing up a little.
直到现在，我都快要热泪盈眶了。

11
00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:38.800
It's so good to be back.
能回来真好。

12
00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:40.540
It's so good to be back, lady.
能回来真好，姐妹。

13
00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:41.280
Aw.
噢。

14
00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:44.300
Today, we're talking about Double Date.
今天，我们要聊的是《双重约会》这一集。

15
00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:47.060
It is Season 6, Episode 9.
这是第六季第九集。

16
00:00:47.320 --> 00:00:54.120
It's written by Charlie Grandy, who is the writer famous for Boom Roasted.
编剧是查理·格兰迪，他因写出“Boom Roasted”那段台词而闻名。

17
00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:54.940
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

18
00:00:55.260 --> 00:00:57.340
And directed by Seth Gordon.
导演是塞斯·戈登。

19
00:00:57.700 --> 00:00:58.920
Here's your summary.
这是剧情梗概。

20
00:00:59.340 --> 00:01:06.460
Jim, Pam, Michael, and Pam's mom, Helene, all go out to lunch to celebrate Helene's birthday.
吉姆、帕姆、迈克尔和帕姆的妈妈海伦一起去吃午餐，庆祝海伦的生日。

21
00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:09.460
This is the double date of double date.
这就是名副其实的“双重约会”。

22
00:01:09.660 --> 00:01:10.120
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

23
00:01:10.820 --> 00:01:18.540
And it all goes well until Michael spirals out about Helene's real age, and then he breaks up with her at her birthday lunch.
一切都很顺利，直到迈克尔因为海伦的真实年龄而情绪失控，并在她的生日午餐上和她分手了。

24
00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:19.620
Oh, Michael.
噢，迈克尔。

25
00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:28.420
Meanwhile, Dwight does nice things for everyone in the office in an attempt to get each of them to owe him a favor.
与此同时，德怀特在办公室里对每个人都很好，试图让每个人都欠他一个人情。

26
00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:31.940
Then he's going to cash in his favors to get Jim fired.
然后他打算利用这些人情让吉姆被解雇。

27
00:01:32.440 --> 00:01:36.940
But unfortunately for Dwight, Andy is also very good at favors.
但不幸的是，安迪也非常擅长处理人情往来。

28
00:01:37.340 --> 00:01:39.080
Andy will not owe you anything.
安迪绝不会欠你任何东西。

29
00:01:39.080 --> 00:01:44.720
I love it when he's like, you send me a wedding invitation, I respond.
我喜欢他那种感觉，比如你给他发婚礼请柬，他就会回复。

30
00:01:45.080 --> 00:01:45.520
Yes.
没错。

31
00:01:45.800 --> 00:01:47.760
Invite me to your birthday, boom, accepted.
邀请他参加生日派对，砰，接受邀请。

32
00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:48.660
Yes.
没错。

33
00:01:48.780 --> 00:01:48.960
Yeah.
是啊。

34
00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:50.920
I would like that.
我喜欢这样。

35
00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:51.560
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

36
00:01:51.700 --> 00:01:52.600
It's a good quality.
这是一种很好的品质。

37
00:01:52.900 --> 00:01:56.540
I mean, you know, you probably get a handwritten thank you card from Andy.
我是说，你知道的，你可能会收到安迪亲手写的感谢卡。

38
00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:57.340
You probably do.
你很可能会收到。

39
00:01:58.380 --> 00:02:00.520
All right, let's get into fast facts.
好了，让我们进入快速事实环节。

40
00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:05.140
Fast fact number one is all about our director, Seth Gordon.
第一个快速事实是关于我们的导演塞斯·戈登的。

41
00:02:05.140 --> 00:02:13.440
You know, we said last week, we're going to get into some of these, like, heavy hitter directors, and Seth is another one.
你知道，我们上周说过，我们要聊聊这些大牌导演，塞斯就是其中之一。

42
00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:25.260
I loved Seth because he directed one of my favorite movies of all time, the documentary King of Kong, A Fistful of Quarters.
我非常喜欢塞斯，因为他执导了我最喜欢的电影之一，纪录片《金刚：一把四分之一硬币》。

43
00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:27.780
It's so flippin' good.
那部片子简直太棒了。

44
00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:32.360
It's so good, and we re-watched it as a family.
真的太棒了，我们全家又重看了一遍。

45
00:02:32.540 --> 00:02:33.120
Did you?
真的吗？

46
00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:34.280
With the kids.
和孩子们一起。

47
00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:38.000
If you do not know this documentary, you need to watch it immediately.
如果你还没看过这部纪录片，一定要立刻去看。

48
00:02:38.320 --> 00:02:42.220
It is about the world of competitive arcade gaming.
它讲述的是竞技街机游戏的世界。

49
00:02:43.340 --> 00:02:49.100
Specifically, it follows this just gentle-hearted...
具体来说，它追踪了一位心地善良的……

50
00:02:49.100 --> 00:02:50.160
Sweet guy.
可爱的人。

51
00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:56.180
...named Steve Wiebe in his attempt to beat the Donkey Kong high score,
……名叫史蒂夫·韦比，他试图打破《大金刚》的最高分纪录，

52
00:02:57.100 --> 00:03:02.380
which was held for, like, 20 years by this guy, Billy Mitchell.
这个纪录由一个叫比利·米切尔的人保持了大概20年。

53
00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:03.360
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

54
00:03:03.740 --> 00:03:07.900
Billy Mitchell is, like, the ultimate documentary villain.
比利·米切尔简直是纪录片里的终极反派。

55
00:03:08.820 --> 00:03:15.900
The story of these two guys battling it out to have the high score on Donkey Kong, I couldn't love him more.
这两个人为了争夺《大金刚》最高分而展开较量的故事，我真是太喜欢了。

56
00:03:16.060 --> 00:03:18.840
When he would go in his garage and practice...
当他走进车库练习的时候……

57
00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:19.220
Yes.
没错。

58
00:03:19.480 --> 00:03:21.560
...and his wife would, like, check in...
……他妻子过来看看他的时候……

59
00:03:21.560 --> 00:03:22.200
I know.
我知道。

60
00:03:22.420 --> 00:03:23.120
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

61
00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:25.560
You guys, it is such a wonderful story.
伙计们，这真是一个精彩的故事。

62
00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:29.120
You can find it on Prime Video and Apple TV.
你们可以在Prime Video和Apple TV上找到它。

63
00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:30.700
We watched on Prime.
我们在Prime上看的。

64
00:03:30.840 --> 00:03:31.480
We had to buy it.
我们还得花钱买来看。

65
00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:33.200
I'm so glad we did.
我很高兴我们买了。

66
00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:36.800
So, Seth Gordon, he did everything on this movie.
所以，塞斯·戈登，他包办了这部电影的一切。

67
00:03:36.940 --> 00:03:37.600
He directed it.
他担任导演。

68
00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:38.740
He was the cinematographer.
他担任摄影指导。

69
00:03:38.740 --> 00:03:39.880
He edited it.
他负责剪辑。

70
00:03:40.580 --> 00:03:42.280
And then he came and did our show.
后来他还来参加了我们的节目。

71
00:03:42.420 --> 00:03:44.920
So, we got another documentary and film director.
所以，我们又迎来了一位纪录片和电影导演。

72
00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:47.840
I looked through my digital clutter, lady.
我翻了翻我的数字杂物，女士。

73
00:03:48.180 --> 00:03:48.600
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

74
00:03:48.740 --> 00:03:54.120
And I actually emailed a friend of mine saying how excited I was to have Seth on set.
我确实给朋友发了封邮件，说我有多兴奋能请到塞斯来片场。

75
00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:54.620
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

76
00:03:54.720 --> 00:03:56.580
And that we were all really excited.
而且我们所有人都非常兴奋。

77
00:03:56.820 --> 00:04:00.980
And then I also said, and I have a day off because...
然后我还说，我那天正好休息，因为……

78
00:04:00.980 --> 00:04:02.860
Because of the double date storyline.
因为那个双重约会的剧情线。

79
00:04:03.240 --> 00:04:03.740
The double date story.
双重约会的故事。

80
00:04:03.960 --> 00:04:05.600
And guess what I did with my day off?
你猜我休息那天做了什么？

81
00:04:05.720 --> 00:04:06.040
What?
什么？

82
00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:08.420
I did an episode of Yo Gabba Gabba.
我录了一集《Yo Gabba Gabba》。

83
00:04:08.420 --> 00:04:10.320
Oh, I remember that, Ange.
哦，我记得那个，安吉。

84
00:04:10.320 --> 00:04:12.280
Yeah, because my daughter loved the show.
是啊，因为我女儿很喜欢那个节目。

85
00:04:12.280 --> 00:04:13.360
And I went to the set.
我去了片场。

86
00:04:13.460 --> 00:04:14.700
I got to play the school teacher.
我有幸扮演了学校老师。

87
00:04:15.080 --> 00:04:17.080
I had to sing about show and tell.
我得唱关于“展示与讲述”的歌。

88
00:04:17.580 --> 00:04:18.440
Here it is.
就是这个。

89
00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:21.500
Show and tell.
展示与讲述。

90
00:04:26.660 --> 00:04:28.080
Gosh, well done, Angela.
天哪，干得好，安吉拉。

91
00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:29.540
Time for show and tell.
到了展示与讲述的时间了。

92
00:04:29.860 --> 00:04:31.400
I had to sing and dance.
我得又唱又跳。

93
00:04:31.560 --> 00:04:33.180
You know, these are things I do not do.
你知道，这些事我平时是不做的。

94
00:04:33.520 --> 00:04:35.640
But it's what you do for your kids.
但为了孩子，你什么都愿意做。

95
00:04:35.840 --> 00:04:36.800
Isabel's so excited.
伊莎贝尔太兴奋了。

96
00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:41.820
They gave me this great picture of her and I on set with all of the characters.
他们给了我一张很棒的照片，是我和她在片场与所有角色的合影。

97
00:04:41.860 --> 00:04:43.180
And I have it in my office.
我把它放在我的办公室里。

98
00:04:43.480 --> 00:04:44.520
It's so cute.
太可爱了。

99
00:04:44.520 --> 00:04:47.260
And everyone there was so nice.
那里每个人都特别好。

100
00:04:47.440 --> 00:04:48.520
They were so much fun.
他们真的很有趣。

101
00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:51.760
It was one of the most fun days of work I've ever had.
那是我工作以来最开心的一天之一。

102
00:04:52.240 --> 00:04:54.440
Every day on Yo Gabba Gabba was a theme day.
《Yo Gabba Gabba》节目组每天都有一个主题日。

103
00:04:54.980 --> 00:04:56.820
And that day was birthday day.
而那天的主题是生日。

104
00:04:56.960 --> 00:05:00.520
And you would come dressed as whatever your interpretation of that was.
你可以根据自己对主题的理解来打扮。

105
00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:03.020
And this one gal came dressed as a cake.
有个姑娘打扮成了一个蛋糕。

106
00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:04.500
Like fully a cake.
真的是完全把自己装扮成了蛋糕。

107
00:05:04.980 --> 00:05:06.540
Like a hat and a skirt.
戴着帽子，穿着裙子。

108
00:05:06.680 --> 00:05:07.800
But she was a tiered cake.
而且她还是个多层蛋糕。

109
00:05:08.360 --> 00:05:09.580
You would wear that.
你居然会穿成那样。

110
00:05:09.880 --> 00:05:11.000
You love a birthday.
你很喜欢生日吧。

111
00:05:11.300 --> 00:05:12.420
I do love a birthday.
我确实很喜欢生日。

112
00:05:12.860 --> 00:05:17.040
Should we start having theme days on our tape days here at Office Ladies?
我们要不要也在《办公室女士》的录制日搞点主题日活动？

113
00:05:18.060 --> 00:05:19.240
Is that a lot of pressure?
那会不会压力很大？

114
00:05:19.620 --> 00:05:20.720
It feels like a lot of pressure.
感觉压力挺大的。

115
00:05:20.920 --> 00:05:21.100
Okay.
好吧。

116
00:05:21.180 --> 00:05:21.900
We won't do it.
那我们就不搞了。

117
00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:22.800
Maybe once.
或许可以搞一次。

118
00:05:23.020 --> 00:05:24.240
We'll do one theme day.
我们就搞一个主题日。

119
00:05:24.380 --> 00:05:24.760
We'll do one.
就搞一次。

120
00:05:24.880 --> 00:05:26.340
Sam, you have to participate.
山姆，你必须参加。

121
00:05:26.700 --> 00:05:27.200
Everyone participates.
每个人都要参加。

122
00:05:28.020 --> 00:05:28.920
I would love to.
我很乐意。

123
00:05:29.240 --> 00:05:29.400
Okay.
好的。

124
00:05:30.460 --> 00:05:31.400
Theme day coming up.
主题日安排上了。

125
00:05:31.400 --> 00:05:34.620
Well, before we move to Fast Fact No.
好了，在进入第二个速览事实之前，

126
00:05:34.680 --> 00:05:40.100
2, let me also add that Seth Gordon has gone on to direct huge movies.
我还想补充一点，塞斯·戈登后来执导了很多大片。

127
00:05:40.460 --> 00:05:45.260
Four Christmases, Horrible Bosses, Identity Theft, and Baywatch.
比如《四个圣诞节》、《恶老板》、《身份窃贼》和《海滩救护队》。

128
00:05:45.640 --> 00:05:47.700
He's also directed a ton of television.
他还执导了大量的电视剧。

129
00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:49.600
I loved working with him.
我非常喜欢和他合作。

130
00:05:49.660 --> 00:05:50.620
I loved him.
我很喜欢他。

131
00:05:50.620 --> 00:05:53.440
So now, Fast Fact No.
那么现在，第二个速览事实是关于拍摄地点的解析。

132
00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:56.940
2 is a location breakdown.
是关于那家餐厅的吗？

133
00:05:57.360 --> 00:05:58.980
Is it of the restaurant?
是的。

134
00:05:59.220 --> 00:05:59.700
Yes.
我是说，这一集里有很大一部分戏份都是在那个叫“Paparazzo's”的餐厅里拍摄的。

135
00:06:00.060 --> 00:06:05.580
I mean, so much of this episode takes place at this restaurant, Paparazzo's.
那不是一家真实的餐厅。

136
00:06:06.320 --> 00:06:07.840
Not a real restaurant.
是我们虚构出来的。

137
00:06:08.230 --> 00:06:09.140
We made it up.
我们是在洛杉矶摄影棚城一家叫“Bistro Garden”的地方拍摄的。

138
00:06:09.440 --> 00:06:15.580
We filmed it in Los Angeles at this place called Bistro Garden in Studio City.
我正想说，等等，我开车经过那里。

139
00:06:15.580 --> 00:06:17.760
I was going to say, wait, I've driven past that.
没错，我在那儿吃过饭。

140
00:06:17.940 --> 00:06:19.260
Yeah, I've eaten there.
它就在冷水峡谷大道和文图拉大道的交汇处。

141
00:06:19.660 --> 00:06:22.220
It's at the corner of Coldwater and Ventura.
哦，对，就是那个有大遮阳篷和台阶的地方。

142
00:06:22.720 --> 00:06:25.980
Oh, yeah, with the big awning and the steps.
没错。

143
00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:26.520
Yes.
是的。

144
00:06:26.580 --> 00:06:26.900
Yes.
是的。

145
00:06:27.380 --> 00:06:30.340
It's now closed, but it was a really great restaurant.
它现在已经关门了，但那真是一家很棒的餐厅。

146
00:06:30.820 --> 00:06:37.980
When I reached out to our writer on this episode, Charlie Grandy, to ask him about some of his memories that we might be able to share,
当我联系这一集的编剧查理·格兰迪，问他有没有什么我们可以分享的回忆时，

147
00:06:37.980 --> 00:06:49.980
he reminded me that there was a giant water main break on Coldwater Canyon Road that exploded and flooded the whole area.
他提醒我，当时冷水峡谷大道上的一根巨大水管爆裂，导致整个区域被淹。

148
00:06:50.440 --> 00:06:50.620
Yes.
没错。

149
00:06:50.800 --> 00:06:52.000
I remember that.
我记得那件事。

150
00:06:52.300 --> 00:06:56.800
And that was like the day before we were supposed to shoot in this area.
那好像就在我们原定要在该区域拍摄的前一天发生的。

151
00:06:57.380 --> 00:07:00.560
I used to live off this road, off Coldwater Canyon.
我以前住在这条路附近，就在冷水峡谷那边。

152
00:07:00.860 --> 00:07:07.620
There was one way in and one way out of my neighborhood, and it was this road where this water main broke.
我住的社区只有一条路进出，就是这条水管爆裂的路。

153
00:07:08.540 --> 00:07:15.560
Randy Cordray confirmed that this happened, and it caused a huge problem with this intersection.
兰迪·科德雷证实了这件事，它导致这个路口出现了大问题。

154
00:07:15.860 --> 00:07:18.860
There were hundreds of thousands of gallons of water.
当时有几十万加仑的水涌了出来。

155
00:07:19.410 --> 00:07:21.260
It was about four feet deep.
水深大约有四英尺。

156
00:07:21.600 --> 00:07:23.120
There was all this traffic.
到处都是车流。

157
00:07:23.320 --> 00:07:24.880
It took like three days to clean it up.
清理工作花了大概三天时间。

158
00:07:24.980 --> 00:07:26.900
Some guy had to be rescued from his car.
有个家伙不得不从车里被救出来。

159
00:07:27.460 --> 00:07:37.740
All the businesses along that street flooded and had to be closed, and some of them had to be renovated, and some didn't even come back because it was too much damage.
沿街所有的商家都被淹了，不得不关门，有些还得重新装修，甚至有些因为损失太严重直接倒闭了。

160
00:07:38.160 --> 00:07:39.660
And you know what I remember?
你知道我记得什么吗？

161
00:07:40.380 --> 00:07:45.880
I remember right on Coldwater, a few days after the flood, there was a sinkhole.
我记得就在冷水峡谷路边，洪水过后几天，出现了一个天坑。

162
00:07:46.260 --> 00:07:46.780
Yes.
没错。

163
00:07:47.040 --> 00:07:49.240
And they had a giant hole in the ground.
地上有个巨大的坑。

164
00:07:49.600 --> 00:07:51.380
Lady, I found a picture of it.
女士，我找到了当时的照片。

165
00:07:51.540 --> 00:07:52.860
This was in the L.A.
那是《洛杉矶时报》上的。

166
00:07:52.960 --> 00:07:53.280
Times.
时报。

167
00:07:53.740 --> 00:07:54.260
Yes.
是的。

168
00:07:54.400 --> 00:07:55.740
It was crazy.
太疯狂了。

169
00:07:55.940 --> 00:08:01.580
And then they had to fix the sinkhole by laying these big metal plate things on the ground.
后来他们不得不通过在地上铺设那些大金属板来修复天坑。

170
00:08:01.580 --> 00:08:03.900
And when you drove over them, it was like, ka-junk, ka-junk.
当你开车经过时，会发出“哐当、哐当”的声音。

171
00:08:04.100 --> 00:08:04.380
Yeah.
是啊。

172
00:08:04.380 --> 00:08:05.340
It was scary.
挺吓人的。

173
00:08:06.300 --> 00:08:13.460
And then later, they had to fix this water main, and you had to have a special pass to even drive on this road.
后来他们还得维修这条水管，你甚至得有特别通行证才能在这条路上开车。

174
00:08:13.620 --> 00:08:18.560
You had to prove that you were a resident with only this road to access your home.
你必须证明你是住户，而且只能通过这条路回家。

175
00:08:18.560 --> 00:08:21.020
So we got the special car passes.
所以我们拿到了特别通行证。

176
00:08:21.420 --> 00:08:23.940
The traffic was a son of a bull.
那交通简直糟糕透了。

177
00:08:24.240 --> 00:08:24.960
It was.
确实。

178
00:08:25.640 --> 00:08:35.420
Amazingly enough, the bistro where we were shooting did not flood, and they found a way that we could access it from this back road, and we still shot that day.
令人惊讶的是，我们拍摄的那家小酒馆没有被淹，他们找到了一条从后路进入的方法，所以那天我们照常拍摄了。

179
00:08:36.180 --> 00:08:36.780
Wow.
哇。

180
00:08:37.080 --> 00:08:37.260
Yeah.
是啊。

181
00:08:37.960 --> 00:08:38.520
All right.
好吧。

182
00:08:38.720 --> 00:08:40.380
Fast fact number three, Angela.
第三个冷知识，安吉拉。

183
00:08:40.660 --> 00:08:40.940
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

184
00:08:41.300 --> 00:08:47.940
The other memory that Charlie Grandy shared was that he got a BlackBerry during this episode.
查理·格兰迪分享的另一个记忆是，他在这一集拍摄期间买了部黑莓手机。

185
00:08:48.320 --> 00:08:53.300
He finally upgraded his flip phone, but he said he did not know how to set it up.
他终于把翻盖手机换掉了，但他说是真的不知道怎么设置。

186
00:08:54.560 --> 00:08:58.400
So he asked John to help him.
于是他找约翰帮忙。

187
00:08:58.540 --> 00:09:00.220
To set up his BlackBerry on set?
在片场设置他的黑莓手机？

188
00:09:01.240 --> 00:09:04.660
Because John was the voice of BlackBerry.
因为约翰是黑莓手机的代言人。

189
00:09:04.840 --> 00:09:05.240
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

190
00:09:05.400 --> 00:09:06.220
John had one.
约翰有一部。

191
00:09:06.400 --> 00:09:10.100
He had to know how to use it because he was, like, part of a campaign.
他必须得知道怎么用，因为他算是广告活动的一部分。

192
00:09:10.440 --> 00:09:10.720
Yeah.
没错。

193
00:09:11.100 --> 00:09:12.500
I found an audio clip.
我找到了一段音频剪辑。

194
00:09:12.840 --> 00:09:13.100
Oh.
哦。

195
00:09:14.380 --> 00:09:15.160
What's this?
这是什么？

196
00:09:15.380 --> 00:09:16.460
The new BlackBerry?
新款黑莓手机？

197
00:09:16.460 --> 00:09:18.160
You've seen BlackBerrys before.
你以前见过黑莓手机吧。

198
00:09:18.420 --> 00:09:18.940
It's no big deal.
没什么大不了的。

199
00:09:19.560 --> 00:09:23.040
Maybe one quick peek just to see what all the fuss is about.
也许可以快速瞄一眼，看看大家都在大惊小怪什么。

200
00:09:23.880 --> 00:09:24.320
Whoa.
哇。

201
00:09:26.980 --> 00:09:27.560
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

202
00:09:27.760 --> 00:09:34.840
So this was when BlackBerry was getting away from the little buttons, and they were just, like, going to become a touchscreen BlackBerry.
当时黑莓正准备放弃小按键，打算转型做触屏黑莓手机。

203
00:09:34.980 --> 00:09:36.120
So that's why he's like, whoa.
所以他才会那样，哇哦。

204
00:09:36.740 --> 00:09:38.560
He has a really good voice for that.
他的声音真的很适合做这个。

205
00:09:38.720 --> 00:09:40.400
He's done tons of voiceovers.
他做过很多配音工作。

206
00:09:40.400 --> 00:09:40.760
I know.
我知道。

207
00:09:41.140 --> 00:09:49.540
So anyway, I loved that Charlie had a memory that during different setups, he'd be, like, getting John to set up his new BlackBerry for him.
总之，我特别喜欢查理的一段记忆，在不同的拍摄间隙，他会找约翰帮他设置新黑莓手机。

208
00:09:50.240 --> 00:09:57.360
It's so funny because, you know, like, when you're talking to someone and they all of a sudden tell you something and all of these memories flood back?
这太搞笑了，你知道吗，就像当你和某人聊天时，他们突然告诉你某件事，然后所有的记忆都涌上心头？

209
00:09:57.480 --> 00:09:57.660
Yeah.
是啊。

210
00:09:57.660 --> 00:10:00.020
So that's now happened twice today.
今天已经发生两次这种情况了。

211
00:10:00.280 --> 00:10:01.400
First of all, the sinkhole.
首先是那个天坑。

212
00:10:01.600 --> 00:10:02.660
I remember the sinkhole.
我还记得那个天坑。

213
00:10:03.200 --> 00:10:07.000
Secondly, I remember getting my BlackBerry and having Rain help me.
其次，我记得我拿到黑莓手机时，是雷恩帮我的。

214
00:10:07.740 --> 00:10:07.960
Yeah.
是啊。

215
00:10:08.160 --> 00:10:11.820
Rain got so frustrated with me because he was like, Angela, you're not listening.
雷恩当时对我特别无语，他说，安吉拉，你根本没在听。

216
00:10:13.920 --> 00:10:16.180
Yeah, because Rain was the first one to get one.
是啊，因为雷恩是第一个拿到手机的人。

217
00:10:16.300 --> 00:10:16.500
Yeah.
没错。

218
00:10:16.840 --> 00:10:19.760
But I just remember Rain helped me set up my BlackBerry.
但我只记得是雷恩帮我设置的黑莓手机。

219
00:10:20.080 --> 00:10:22.820
Well, that's all I got for Fast Facts.
好了，我的“快速事实”就这些了。

220
00:10:23.300 --> 00:10:24.620
Well, I loved your Fast Facts.
我很喜欢你的“快速事实”。

221
00:10:24.720 --> 00:10:27.980
They took me down memory lane, and this is such a fun episode.
它们带我重温了往事，这一集真的太有趣了。

222
00:10:27.980 --> 00:10:29.540
I was so delighted by it.
我感到非常高兴。

223
00:10:29.680 --> 00:10:31.880
I can't wait for us to just get right into it.
我迫不及待想让我们直接进入正题了。

224
00:10:32.040 --> 00:10:35.660
I had forgotten about so much of it, so I loved it, too.
我把很多细节都忘了，所以我也很喜欢这些内容。

225
00:10:35.960 --> 00:10:37.060
Well, how about this?
那这样如何？

226
00:10:37.180 --> 00:10:41.980
Let's go to break, because when we come back, lady, I brought in one of my journals.
我们先休息一下，因为回来之后，女士，我带了一本我的日记。

227
00:10:42.740 --> 00:10:43.140
Oh!
噢！

228
00:10:43.460 --> 00:10:43.840
Oh!
噢！

229
00:10:45.160 --> 00:10:47.000
This day is awesome.
今天真是太棒了。

230
00:10:47.260 --> 00:10:48.760
Things are going to get spicy.
接下来要变得火辣起来了。

231
00:10:58.260 --> 00:10:59.300
We are back.
我们回来了。

232
00:10:59.300 --> 00:11:04.960
Dwight is walking around with, I want you to know, what I think was a very nice basket,
德怀特走来走去，我想让你知道，他拿的那个篮子我觉得非常漂亮，

233
00:11:05.260 --> 00:11:08.300
because I notice a basket.
因为我注意到了那个篮子。

234
00:11:08.760 --> 00:11:15.160
He's got all of these beautiful bagels from H&H Bagel in New York, and he has started his
他带了好多来自纽约 H&H Bagel 的美味贝果，而且他已经开启了他的

235
00:11:15.160 --> 00:11:16.320
favorite campaign.
最爱活动。

236
00:11:17.340 --> 00:11:17.640
Yeah.
是啊。

237
00:11:18.000 --> 00:11:22.000
I'll have you know, H&H Bagels is a real place in New York.
我要告诉你，H&H Bagels 是纽约真实存在的地方。

238
00:11:22.280 --> 00:11:25.040
It's very famous for having the best bagels.
它以拥有最好的贝果而闻名。

239
00:11:25.040 --> 00:11:30.940
And this is also not the first time that H&H Bagels has been featured on a television show.
而且这也不是 H&H Bagels 第一次在电视节目中亮相了。

240
00:11:31.380 --> 00:11:32.540
What was the other show?
另一部剧是什么？

241
00:11:33.080 --> 00:11:33.600
Seinfeld.
《宋飞正传》。

242
00:11:33.900 --> 00:11:34.760
Oh, yeah.
噢，对。

243
00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:36.260
And I have an audio clip.
我还有一段音频剪辑。

244
00:11:36.500 --> 00:11:37.340
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

245
00:11:38.620 --> 00:11:39.340
Great news.
好消息。

246
00:11:39.840 --> 00:11:41.220
Yeah, the strike's been settled.
是啊，罢工解决了。

247
00:11:41.300 --> 00:11:42.580
I'm going back to work.
我要回去工作了。

248
00:11:43.600 --> 00:11:44.380
What's the other guy?
另一个人是谁？

249
00:11:44.540 --> 00:11:45.300
H&H Bagels.
H&H Bagels。

250
00:11:45.440 --> 00:11:46.220
That's where I worked.
那就是我工作的地方。

251
00:11:46.440 --> 00:11:47.340
You worked?
你工作过？

252
00:11:48.260 --> 00:11:48.620
Bagels?
百吉饼？

253
00:11:48.720 --> 00:11:49.220
Yeah, look, see?
是啊，你看，看到了吗？

254
00:11:49.400 --> 00:11:50.640
I still have my business card.
我还有我的名片呢。

255
00:11:51.080 --> 00:11:53.120
Yeah, we've been on strike for 12 years.
是啊，我们已经罢工12年了。

256
00:11:54.040 --> 00:11:58.040
I remember seeing those guys picketing out there, but I haven't seen them in a long time.
我记得以前见过那些人在外面抗议，但我已经很久没见过他们了。

257
00:11:58.200 --> 00:12:01.500
Yeah, well, H&H wouldn't let us use their bathroom while we were picketing.
是啊，H&H在我们抗议的时候不让我们用他们的洗手间。

258
00:12:02.300 --> 00:12:03.920
Put a crimp in our solidarity.
这严重打击了我们的团结。

259
00:12:05.980 --> 00:12:07.820
What are your demands?
你们的要求是什么？

260
00:12:08.340 --> 00:12:11.260
Yeah, $5.35 an hour, and that's what they're paying now.
是啊，时薪5.35美元，他们现在给的就是这个数。

261
00:12:11.740 --> 00:12:14.260
I believe that's the new minimum wage.
我想那应该是新的最低工资标准。

262
00:12:14.500 --> 00:12:15.860
And now you know who to thank for that.
现在你知道该感谢谁了吧。

263
00:12:16.760 --> 00:12:17.920
All right, I gotta go.
好了，我得走了。

264
00:12:18.200 --> 00:12:20.100
Why didn't you ever mention this?
你为什么从来没提过这件事？

265
00:12:20.760 --> 00:12:22.900
Jerry, I didn't want you to know I was out of work.
杰瑞，我不想让你知道我失业了。

266
00:12:23.160 --> 00:12:24.120
It's embarrassing.
这很丢人。

267
00:12:26.570 --> 00:12:36.850
So this is the storyline that suddenly you find out that Kramer had a job, that he's been on strike, and it was H&H Bagels, and he goes back to the bagel place,
所以剧情是这样的，你突然发现克莱默以前有份工作，他一直在罢工，而且是在H&H百吉饼店，然后他回到了那家店，

268
00:12:36.850 --> 00:12:38.490
and he gets his job back.
又重新得到了那份工作。

269
00:12:38.530 --> 00:12:43.390
But he doesn't know, like, he gets there, and I ended up watching the episode.
但他不知道，比如，他到了那里，我最后看了那一集。

270
00:12:43.470 --> 00:12:44.190
I can't tell.
我看不出来。

271
00:12:44.890 --> 00:12:48.610
And he gets there, and he's like, raisin bagel?
他到了那里，他说，葡萄干百吉饼？

272
00:12:48.970 --> 00:12:50.690
We're putting raisins in them.
我们要在里面加葡萄干。

273
00:12:50.810 --> 00:12:53.370
And you're like, yeah, I mean, the raisin bagel.
然后你就会说，对啊，我是说，葡萄干百吉饼。

274
00:12:53.450 --> 00:12:54.630
He's like, all right, I can do it.
他说，好吧，我能做。

275
00:12:55.010 --> 00:12:56.090
It was very funny.
那段非常搞笑。

276
00:12:56.350 --> 00:13:02.490
But I'll have you know that the bagels that Dwight is passing out were not actually H&H Bagels from New York.
但我得告诉你，德怀特分发的那些百吉饼其实并不是纽约的H&H百吉饼。

277
00:13:02.630 --> 00:13:05.790
They were from a place called Western Bagel in Vinay's.
它们来自维奈的一家叫西部百吉饼的店。

278
00:13:06.390 --> 00:13:07.990
Western Bagel's very good, too.
西部百吉饼也很好吃。

279
00:13:08.030 --> 00:13:08.890
I've been there.
我去过那里。

280
00:13:09.410 --> 00:13:11.770
I have a little something to share about H&H.
关于H&H，我有一点小事要分享。

281
00:13:11.770 --> 00:13:12.750
What is it?
什么事？

282
00:13:12.850 --> 00:13:14.170
Why are you reaching in a bag?
你为什么往包里掏东西？

283
00:13:14.350 --> 00:13:15.510
I'm reaching for my journal.
我在掏我的日记本。

284
00:13:16.090 --> 00:13:16.490
What?
什么？

285
00:13:16.810 --> 00:13:17.370
Get ready.
准备好了。

286
00:13:17.830 --> 00:13:18.350
Okay.
好的。

287
00:13:18.690 --> 00:13:25.990
The first bagel I ever had was an H&H Bagel, and it was when I was interning on Late Night with Conan O'Brien.
我吃过的第一个百吉饼就是H&H百吉饼，那是我在《柯南·奥布莱恩深夜秀》实习的时候。

288
00:13:26.530 --> 00:13:28.070
Stop it right now.
快停下。

289
00:13:28.250 --> 00:13:31.670
This journal, it's a flower journal.
这本日记本，是个花朵图案的日记本。

290
00:13:32.030 --> 00:13:34.790
It has many Post-it notes sticking out of it.
上面贴着很多便利贴。

291
00:13:34.870 --> 00:13:35.970
Pages are falling out.
书页都要掉出来了。

292
00:13:36.170 --> 00:13:39.330
And there is a Late Night with Conan O'Brien sticker.
上面还有一个《柯南·奥布莱恩深夜秀》的贴纸。

293
00:13:39.330 --> 00:13:43.390
I got the sticker when I got the internship, and I put it on my journal.
我得到实习机会时拿到了这个贴纸，然后把它贴在了我的日记本上。

294
00:13:43.550 --> 00:13:46.130
I mean, I'm taking a picture of you, obviously.
我是说，我显然是在给你拍照。

295
00:13:47.250 --> 00:13:47.570
All right.
好吧。

296
00:13:47.650 --> 00:13:53.370
Before we turn to the page where I talk about my first bagel experience, I interned on Conan O'Brien.
在我们翻到我记录第一次吃百吉饼经历的那一页之前，我曾在柯南·奥布莱恩那里实习。

297
00:13:54.310 --> 00:13:58.970
Years later, over a decade later, I was asked to be a gueSt.
多年以后，十多年后，我被邀请去做嘉宾。

298
00:13:58.970 --> 00:14:05.350
It was a full-circle life moment because I went from the person who was getting everyone's coffee to actually being a gueSt.
那是一个圆满的人生时刻，因为我从那个帮大家买咖啡的人，变成了真正的嘉宾。

299
00:14:05.890 --> 00:14:11.950
And I brought my journal when I was a guest, and I read this on Late Night with Conan.
我做嘉宾时带上了我的日记本，并在《柯南深夜秀》上读了这段内容。

300
00:14:12.510 --> 00:14:13.070
Ready?
准备好了吗？

301
00:14:13.370 --> 00:14:13.810
Yes.
是的。

302
00:14:14.030 --> 00:14:14.790
I cannot wait.
我等不及了。

303
00:14:15.170 --> 00:14:16.350
Turning to the page.
翻到这一页。

304
00:14:16.510 --> 00:14:17.270
Here we go.
开始了。

305
00:14:18.070 --> 00:14:22.930
Tomorrow night is Conan's first-year anniversary party at the Museum of Modern Art.
明晚是柯南在现代艺术博物馆举办的一周年纪念派对。

306
00:14:22.930 --> 00:14:28.890
Lots of important people, stars, NBC folks, and the interns get to go.
会有很多重要人物、明星、NBC的工作人员，实习生也能去。

307
00:14:29.250 --> 00:14:29.790
Wow!
哇！

308
00:14:31.150 --> 00:14:32.270
Details later.
详情稍后。

309
00:14:33.590 --> 00:14:35.650
What are my details later to myself?
我为什么要给自己写“详情稍后”？

310
00:14:35.910 --> 00:14:36.930
This is my journal.
这是我的日记。

311
00:14:37.350 --> 00:14:38.890
I go on to say.
我继续写道。

312
00:14:39.530 --> 00:14:42.610
And there are serious food perks to interning here.
在这里实习还有很棒的伙食福利。

313
00:14:42.830 --> 00:14:46.670
I get a free meal with the writers, and I had my first bagel.
我可以和编剧们一起免费用餐，我还吃了人生中第一个贝果。

