00:22:05.490 --> 00:22:06.170
What's that?
那是什么？

492
00:22:06.390 --> 00:22:08.210
I love a coffee mug callback.
我喜欢咖啡杯的呼应。

493
00:22:08.430 --> 00:22:14.190
Andy has his mug from Kelly's America's Got Talent viewing party sitting on his desk.
安迪桌上放着他在凯莉的《美国达人秀》观看派对上用的那个杯子。

494
00:22:14.690 --> 00:22:18.950
Also, this was not the cold open in the shooting draft.
另外，这并不是拍摄初稿里的冷开场。

495
00:22:19.750 --> 00:22:20.350
Really?
真的吗？

496
00:22:20.750 --> 00:22:22.770
Yeah, there was a whole different cold open.
是的，原本有一个完全不同的冷开场。

497
00:22:23.370 --> 00:22:24.690
Here's what it said.
内容是这样的。

498
00:22:24.990 --> 00:22:27.610
Cold open, interior, Michael's office.
冷开场，内景，迈克尔的办公室。

499
00:22:28.250 --> 00:22:31.890
Michael sits at his desk, flipping through a small stack of pictures.
迈克尔坐在桌前，翻看着一小叠照片。

500
00:22:32.250 --> 00:22:34.050
He sees Jim walking by.
他看到吉姆走过。

501
00:22:35.110 --> 00:22:36.690
Jim, Jim, you have to see this!
吉姆，吉姆，你一定要看看这个！

502
00:22:36.930 --> 00:22:37.810
Regarding the photo.
关于那张照片。

503
00:22:38.130 --> 00:22:39.370
Do you know who that is?
你知道那是谁吗？

504
00:22:39.470 --> 00:22:39.890
Jim.
吉姆。

505
00:22:40.290 --> 00:22:40.730
No.
不知道。

506
00:22:41.110 --> 00:22:41.450
Michael.
迈克尔。

507
00:22:41.710 --> 00:22:42.970
Come on, how can you not tell?
拜托，你怎么会认不出来？

508
00:22:43.070 --> 00:22:44.150
The t-shirt, the jeans!
那件T恤，那条牛仔裤！

509
00:22:44.370 --> 00:22:44.590
Jim.
吉姆。

510
00:22:44.810 --> 00:22:45.730
Is it you?
是你吗？

511
00:22:46.030 --> 00:22:46.530
Michael.
迈克尔。

512
00:22:46.870 --> 00:22:48.670
I'm flattered, but it's Johnny Depp.
我很荣幸，但那是约翰尼·德普。

513
00:22:49.230 --> 00:22:49.730
Jim.
吉姆。

514
00:22:49.970 --> 00:22:50.230
Really?
真的吗？

515
00:22:50.510 --> 00:22:51.650
Where did you take these?
你在哪拍的这些照片？

516
00:22:51.930 --> 00:22:52.430
Michael.
迈克尔。

517
00:22:52.690 --> 00:22:53.990
My condo complex.
我的公寓大楼。

518
00:22:54.850 --> 00:22:55.350
Jim.
吉姆。

519
00:22:55.630 --> 00:22:56.090
Of course.
果然。

520
00:22:56.090 --> 00:22:57.430
And what was he doing there?
那他在那儿干什么？

521
00:22:57.990 --> 00:22:58.470
Michael.
迈克尔。

522
00:22:58.710 --> 00:22:59.970
Keep this on the down low.
这件事你要保密。

523
00:23:00.130 --> 00:23:01.050
But he was moving in.
他搬进来了。

524
00:23:01.810 --> 00:23:02.070
Jim.
吉姆。

525
00:23:02.450 --> 00:23:06.870
Right, because I read in People that Johnny Depp was looking for a two-bedroom in Scranton.
对，因为我在《人物》杂志上读到过，约翰尼·德普正在斯克兰顿找两居室的房子。

526
00:23:07.210 --> 00:23:07.670
Michael.
迈克尔。

527
00:23:07.850 --> 00:23:09.150
I'm totally flipping!
我简直要疯了！

528
00:23:09.510 --> 00:23:11.950
You know my idea for a fourth Pirates movie, right?
你知道我关于第四部《加勒比海盗》的点子吧？

529
00:23:12.970 --> 00:23:15.090
So, this goes on and on.
所以，这事儿还没完。

530
00:23:15.390 --> 00:23:18.570
Michael is convinced that Johnny Depp has moved in and is his neighbor.
迈克尔坚信约翰尼·德普搬进来了，成了他的邻居。

531
00:23:19.270 --> 00:23:25.850
And as it turns out, when he goes to see Johnny Depp's mailbox, it says M.Shulman.
结果呢，当他去查看约翰尼·德普的信箱时，上面写着M.舒尔曼。

532
00:23:26.270 --> 00:23:27.810
So, it's not Johnny Depp.
所以，那根本不是约翰尼·德普。

533
00:23:28.710 --> 00:23:31.370
I'm surprised Michael doesn't think that's an alias.
我很惊讶迈克尔竟然没觉得那是化名。

534
00:23:32.410 --> 00:23:34.510
It is a really funny scene.
那场戏真的很有趣。

535
00:23:34.510 --> 00:23:38.150
And we shot it, and it also includes Michael's impression of Jack Sparrow.
我们拍了那场戏，里面还包括迈克尔模仿杰克船长的片段。

536
00:23:38.350 --> 00:23:39.570
That exists somewhere.
那段素材应该还在某处存着。

537
00:23:40.550 --> 00:23:42.210
You know, this is crazy.
你知道，这太疯狂了。

538
00:23:42.490 --> 00:23:44.330
This is unlocking a memory for me.
这勾起了我的一段回忆。

539
00:23:44.470 --> 00:23:47.210
When we read that at the table read, we all thought that was so funny.
当我们读剧本围读会的时候，大家都觉得那段特别好笑。

540
00:23:47.210 --> 00:23:47.630
Yeah.
没错。

541
00:23:47.970 --> 00:23:48.350
Amazing.
太棒了。

542
00:23:48.870 --> 00:23:50.830
Are we closing out the cold open?
我们要结束开场戏了吗？

543
00:23:51.210 --> 00:23:51.890
That's it.
就是这样。

544
00:23:51.990 --> 00:23:53.090
We're done with the cold open.
开场戏结束了。

545
00:23:53.210 --> 00:23:53.590
All right.
好的。

546
00:23:54.210 --> 00:23:56.170
Let's move in to the episode.
让我们进入正片吧。

547
00:23:56.650 --> 00:23:59.590
Dwight goes up to Pam's desk and offers her a bagel.
德怀特走到帕姆的办公桌前，问她要不要吃贝果。

548
00:23:59.830 --> 00:24:03.050
She doesn't want one because she's having an early lunch.
她不想吃，因为她要提前吃午饭。

549
00:24:03.250 --> 00:24:08.850
And this is when we find out the information that she's going on this double date for her mom's birthday.
就在这时，我们得知了她要去参加她妈妈生日的双重约会的消息。

550
00:24:09.450 --> 00:24:12.270
We had a fan question from Genevieve B.
我们收到了一位粉丝吉纳维芙·B的提问。

551
00:24:12.510 --> 00:24:13.690
in Omaha, Nebraska.
在内布拉斯加州的奥马哈。

552
00:24:14.370 --> 00:24:18.590
Why is Pam wearing such neutral, earthy colors in this episode?
为什么帕姆在这一集里穿得这么素，全是大地色系？

553
00:24:19.330 --> 00:24:22.330
Normally, she would be wearing at least a little pop of color.
平时她至少会穿点亮眼的颜色。

554
00:24:22.490 --> 00:24:27.390
But in this episode, she looks like she's dressing, dare I say, like Dwight.
但这一集里，她看起来穿得，我敢说，像德怀特一样。

555
00:24:28.010 --> 00:24:28.530
What?
什么？

556
00:24:29.230 --> 00:24:30.690
I see what she's saying.
我明白她说的意思。

557
00:24:30.890 --> 00:24:33.490
The color palette is very shrewty.
这配色确实很“德怀特”。

558
00:24:33.930 --> 00:24:39.470
But I also noticed that everything about it was there was no color.
但我也注意到，整套搭配完全没有色彩。

559
00:24:39.690 --> 00:24:42.130
I think Pam is in mourning.
我觉得帕姆是在哀悼。

560
00:24:42.410 --> 00:24:45.350
I think she is going on this double date.
我觉得她要去参加这次双人约会了。

561
00:24:45.510 --> 00:24:48.990
And she like, when she looked in her closet, this is what spoke to her.
当她看着衣柜时，这些衣服就是她的心声。

562
00:24:49.410 --> 00:24:53.970
I have noticed since Pam has become a salesman that her whole outfit has become more muted.
我注意到自从帕姆当上销售员后，她的整体穿搭变得更沉闷了。

563
00:24:54.710 --> 00:24:56.130
There's less pop of color.
亮色变少了。

564
00:24:56.130 --> 00:24:58.270
Yeah, I've noticed that too.
是啊，我也注意到了。

565
00:24:58.550 --> 00:25:00.070
We're going to get it back.
我们会让她恢复过来的。

566
00:25:00.390 --> 00:25:00.690
Okay.
好的。

567
00:25:01.210 --> 00:25:03.590
Ryan is continuing to evolve.
瑞安在持续进化。

568
00:25:03.990 --> 00:25:04.790
Who is Ryan?
瑞安是谁？

569
00:25:05.070 --> 00:25:07.890
He's the hat-wearing glasses guy.
就是那个戴帽子戴眼镜的家伙。

570
00:25:08.070 --> 00:25:09.170
Now he's a photographer.
现在他成了摄影师。

571
00:25:09.470 --> 00:25:12.370
He's showing his portfolio to Aaron.
他正在给艾琳展示他的作品集。

572
00:25:12.370 --> 00:25:16.950
It's a black and white series that he calls Exposure in the Workplace.
那是一个黑白系列，他称之为《职场曝光》。

573
00:25:17.510 --> 00:25:19.330
I wrote down the images I saw.
我记下了我看到的那些照片。

574
00:25:19.690 --> 00:25:20.490
Do tell.
快说说。

575
00:25:21.230 --> 00:25:24.310
One looks like some drains on the side of the building.
一张看起来像是大楼侧面的排水管。

576
00:25:24.610 --> 00:25:24.870
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

577
00:25:25.370 --> 00:25:28.270
Another one is clearly the Dunder Mifflin parking lot.
另一张显然是邓德·米夫林的停车场。

578
00:25:28.450 --> 00:25:32.150
You can see the top of Meredith's van, the hedge, and the sign.
你能看到梅雷迪思的面包车车顶、树篱和招牌。

579
00:25:32.910 --> 00:25:37.450
And then, of course, we have Kelly, nudie from the waist up at her desk.
然后，当然还有凯莉，在办公桌前上半身赤裸。

580
00:25:37.710 --> 00:25:39.950
We had a fan question from Cecilia P.
我们收到一个来自明尼苏达州塞西莉亚·P的粉丝提问。

581
00:25:40.050 --> 00:25:43.830
in Minnesota who would like to know, what is this photo book?
她想知道，这本相册是怎么回事？

582
00:25:44.570 --> 00:25:46.790
How did we take the photo of Mindy?
我们是怎么拍下明迪那张照片的？

583
00:25:47.310 --> 00:25:48.550
I want to know everything.
我想知道所有细节。

584
00:25:49.330 --> 00:25:50.090
Let's hear it.
说来听听。

585
00:25:50.650 --> 00:25:55.590
Well, Randy Cordray told us that all of the photos were shot by our production designer, Michael Gallenberg.
兰迪·科德雷告诉我们，所有照片都是我们的美术指导迈克尔·加伦伯格拍的。

586
00:25:55.870 --> 00:25:57.470
He would do that for the show.
他会为剧组做这些事。

587
00:25:57.650 --> 00:25:59.610
For example, you mentioned that coffee mug.
比如，你提到的那个咖啡杯。

588
00:25:59.810 --> 00:26:04.010
Michael took the pictures of all the cast members that then Phil Shea put on the coffee mugs.
迈克尔拍了所有演员的照片，然后菲尔·谢伊把它们印在咖啡杯上。

589
00:26:04.010 --> 00:26:08.250
He's actually a very talented, real-life, still photographer.
他其实是一位非常有才华的现实生活中的静物摄影师。

590
00:26:08.470 --> 00:26:10.630
So he did all of these photos.
所以这些照片都是他拍的。

591
00:26:11.350 --> 00:26:17.230
And the shoot with Mindy was done with her wearing, like, a flesh-colored bandeau.
拍明迪那场戏时，她穿的是那种肉色的抹胸。

592
00:26:17.450 --> 00:26:18.350
Like a tube top.
就像管状上衣一样。

593
00:26:18.490 --> 00:26:21.670
Yes, because they knew that it would be pixelated later in poSt.
是的，因为他们知道后期会进行像素化处理。

594
00:26:21.930 --> 00:26:23.350
So that's how we did it.
所以我们就是这么做的。

595
00:26:23.730 --> 00:26:26.330
You know, I'm going to bring out this story.
你知道吗，我要讲个故事。

596
00:26:27.130 --> 00:26:32.450
I wasn't planning on it, but this episode feels like, I don't know, it feels like it would be on theme.
我本来没打算讲，但这一集感觉，怎么说呢，感觉很应景。

597
00:26:33.050 --> 00:26:36.890
I wrote about this in my book, The Actor's Life, A Survival Guide.
我在我的书《演员的生活：生存指南》里写过这件事。

598
00:26:37.330 --> 00:26:42.050
The scene with Ryan showing Erin the pictures of, like, Kelly nude.
就是瑞安给艾琳看那些照片的戏，比如凯莉裸体那张。

599
00:26:42.250 --> 00:26:42.550
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

600
00:26:43.230 --> 00:26:53.850
Have I ever told you the story of how I almost joined, like, an international Spice Girls singing group that was actually a front for a call girl service?
我有没有跟你讲过我差点加入一个国际辣妹合唱团的故事，结果那其实是个应召女郎服务的幌子？

601
00:26:54.430 --> 00:26:54.990
What?
什么？

602
00:26:55.510 --> 00:26:56.070
Yeah.
对。

603
00:26:56.490 --> 00:26:59.930
You thought you were auditioning to be in a band?
你以为你是去参加乐队试镜的？

604
00:27:00.290 --> 00:27:01.890
Yeah, a singing group.
是啊，一个歌唱组合。

605
00:27:01.890 --> 00:27:03.690
That's how they hoodwinked the girls?
他们就是这样忽悠那些女孩的？

606
00:27:03.890 --> 00:27:04.210
Yeah.
没错。

607
00:27:04.570 --> 00:27:04.950
Ah!
啊！

608
00:27:05.410 --> 00:27:05.850
Yeah.
是啊。

609
00:27:06.550 --> 00:27:08.770
I've also told this story on Conan.
我也在柯南秀上讲过这个故事。

610
00:27:09.050 --> 00:27:10.030
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

611
00:27:10.530 --> 00:27:12.910
So I moved to L.A.
当时我搬到了洛杉矶。

612
00:27:13.170 --> 00:27:16.690
And, you know, you're just looking for any gig you can get.
你知道的，就是想找任何能做的工作。

613
00:27:16.870 --> 00:27:17.130
Sure.
当然。

614
00:27:17.530 --> 00:27:20.130
My friend was a really talented singer.
我朋友是个非常有天赋的歌手。

615
00:27:20.330 --> 00:27:25.230
And she saw a listing in the newspaper, the free newspaper.
她在报纸上看到了一则广告，就是那种免费报纸。

616
00:27:25.370 --> 00:27:26.790
Okay, red flag number one.
好吧，第一个危险信号。

617
00:27:26.790 --> 00:27:27.330
Correct.
没错。

618
00:27:28.030 --> 00:27:38.670
For singing auditions for a new international Spice Girls-type singing band in this guy's condo.
说是要在一个男人的公寓里为一支新的国际化辣妹合唱团招募成员。

619
00:27:39.070 --> 00:27:40.550
Red flag number two.
第二个危险信号。

620
00:27:40.650 --> 00:27:40.770
Yeah.
是啊。

621
00:27:40.830 --> 00:27:41.930
Audition in a condo.
在公寓里试镜。

622
00:27:42.070 --> 00:27:42.770
Red flag two.
第二个危险信号。

623
00:27:43.410 --> 00:27:45.410
She asked if I would go with her.
她问我愿不愿意陪她一起去。

624
00:27:45.830 --> 00:27:47.130
I said, sure.
我说，当然。

625
00:27:47.210 --> 00:27:48.370
I'll go with you.
我陪你去。

626
00:27:48.630 --> 00:27:56.690
So I stood in line with her, big group of people, went in, she sang, and the guy's like,
于是我就陪她排队，那里有一大群人，进去之后她唱了一段，那个男的就问，

627
00:27:56.690 --> 00:27:58.450
do you sing to me?
你唱歌给我听听？

628
00:27:58.610 --> 00:27:59.670
And I'm like, not really.
我说，不太会。

629
00:27:59.750 --> 00:28:00.150
No.
不。

630
00:28:00.290 --> 00:28:01.650
He's like, well, just sing something.
他说，没事，随便唱点什么。

631
00:28:02.830 --> 00:28:04.770
So I sang Rocky Top.
于是我就唱了《Rocky Top》。

632
00:28:05.530 --> 00:28:06.010
What?
什么？

633
00:28:06.430 --> 00:28:08.150
You know this song, Rocky Top?
你知道这首歌吗，《Rocky Top》？

634
00:28:08.330 --> 00:28:10.490
Like, good old Rocky Top.
就是那首，古老的Rocky Top。

635
00:28:10.710 --> 00:28:11.270
Rocky Top.
Rocky Top。

636
00:28:11.270 --> 00:28:12.650
Rocky Top, Tennessee.
田纳西州的Rocky Top。

637
00:28:13.290 --> 00:28:13.650
That's what you-
这就是你——

638
00:28:13.650 --> 00:28:14.870
Rocky Top, Tennessee.
田纳西州的Rocky Top。

639
00:28:16.010 --> 00:28:16.190
That's what came-
这就是你——

640
00:28:16.190 --> 00:28:17.290
That's what came to your-
这就是你——

641
00:28:17.290 --> 00:28:18.590
That's what came to your-
这就是你——

642
00:28:19.510 --> 00:28:21.390
So I sang Rocky Top.
所以我唱了《Rocky Top》。

643
00:28:22.630 --> 00:28:23.790
Guess what, lady?
你猜怎么着，女士？

644
00:28:23.990 --> 00:28:25.630
You got the part.
你被选中了。

645
00:28:25.770 --> 00:28:26.630
You're in the band.
你加入这个组合了。

646
00:28:26.910 --> 00:28:27.750
I got it.
我被选上了。

647
00:28:27.850 --> 00:28:29.350
With your Rocky Top song.
就凭你那首《Rocky Top》。

648
00:28:29.510 --> 00:28:30.950
I'm the American girl.
我是那个美国女孩。

649
00:28:31.170 --> 00:28:32.250
Red flag number three.
第三个危险信号。

650
00:28:33.710 --> 00:28:34.950
I get a call.
我接到了一个电话。

651
00:28:35.110 --> 00:28:35.730
It's me.
是我。

652
00:28:36.250 --> 00:28:37.430
Imagine my friend.
想象一下我的朋友。

653
00:28:37.430 --> 00:28:40.250
My friend, who's like a professional-level singer.
我的朋友，她唱歌简直是专业水准。

654
00:28:40.530 --> 00:28:40.770
Yeah.
没错。

655
00:28:40.850 --> 00:28:41.790
She didn't get the gig.
她没拿到那个演出机会。

656
00:28:42.110 --> 00:28:42.990
I got it.
我拿到了。

657
00:28:43.150 --> 00:28:45.750
I'm going to be the American girl.
我要去当那个美国女孩了。

658
00:28:45.750 --> 00:28:48.910
Girl, this guy gives me a tape.
天哪，这男的给了我一盘磁带。

