迈克尔说，哈哈，真有趣。

978
00:42:42.110 --> 00:42:43.990
But you can see him trying to do the math.
但你能看出他在努力算这笔账。

979
00:42:44.450 --> 00:42:46.710
But then he's going to need to take pencil to paper.
但他得拿笔在纸上算才行。

980
00:42:47.190 --> 00:42:48.570
And still get it wrong.
而且还是会算错。

981
00:42:48.810 --> 00:42:49.130
Right.
没错。

982
00:42:49.750 --> 00:42:52.370
Michael realizes that Helene is 58.
迈克尔意识到海琳其实是58岁。

983
00:42:52.790 --> 00:42:55.970
And you can tell this hits him pretty hard.
你能看出这对他打击挺大的。

984
00:42:56.230 --> 00:42:58.910
We had a fan catch, though, from Allison H.
不过，我们收到了一位粉丝艾莉森·H的指正，

985
00:42:58.910 --> 00:43:05.590
in Louisville, Kentucky, and many others, by the way, who said, I think there's a math error.
她来自肯塔基州路易斯维尔，顺便说一下，还有许多其他人也指出了，她说，我觉得这里有个数学错误。

986
00:43:06.430 --> 00:43:08.210
Helene says she's 49.
海琳说她49岁。

987
00:43:08.750 --> 00:43:10.990
Pam says it's the ninth year in a row.
帕姆说这是连续第九年了。

988
00:43:11.290 --> 00:43:19.570
But if she first celebrated her 49th birthday on her 49th birthday, that counts as one of the nine.
但如果她第一次庆祝49岁生日是在她49岁那年，那就算作九年中的一年。

989
00:43:19.570 --> 00:43:27.190
So you would actually add 49 plus eight additional birthdays, which means Helene is really turning 57.
所以实际上应该是49加上额外的八个生日，这意味着海琳其实是57岁。

990
00:43:27.970 --> 00:43:29.190
Nice catch.
好眼力。

991
00:43:29.610 --> 00:43:30.050
Yeah.
是啊。

992
00:43:30.350 --> 00:43:41.990
So when I was trading messages with Charlie Grandy about this episode, he said that what he remembers most about working with Seth Gordon was the fact that me, John, Steve,
所以当我和查理·格兰迪交流关于这一集的信息时，他说他关于和塞斯·戈登合作最深刻的记忆是，我和约翰、史蒂夫，

993
00:43:41.990 --> 00:43:47.590
and Linda were going to be locked at this same table for like four big scenes in a row.
还有琳达，要在同一张桌子旁连续拍四场大戏。

994
00:43:48.050 --> 00:43:49.930
And it became this big question.
这成了一个大问题。

995
00:43:50.110 --> 00:43:53.590
How are we going to visually differentiate these scenes?
我们要如何从视觉上区分这些场景呢？

996
00:43:53.770 --> 00:43:56.470
How are we going to make them feel alive?
我们要如何让它们看起来生动有趣？

997
00:43:56.850 --> 00:43:56.990
Right.
没错。

998
00:43:58.090 --> 00:44:02.830
And Charlie said, if you rewatch it, you can really see what a great job he did.
查理说，如果你重看一遍，真的能看出他做得有多棒。

999
00:44:03.030 --> 00:44:04.850
He added multiple angles.
他增加了多个拍摄角度。

1000
00:44:05.170 --> 00:44:07.590
He keeps flipping sides to keep it interesting.
他不断切换拍摄侧面来保持画面的新鲜感。

1001
00:44:07.590 --> 00:44:20.670
And by mostly framing out the other tables, he does a great job of shrinking what was a really big space and, quote, imprisoning you in Michael's awkwardness.
他通过遮挡其他桌子，成功地缩小了原本很大的空间，用他的话说是，把你“囚禁”在迈克尔的尴尬之中。

1002
00:44:21.150 --> 00:44:22.910
Ooh, that's so artsy.
噢，这太有艺术感了。

1003
00:44:23.070 --> 00:44:23.650
I know.
我知道。

1004
00:44:23.650 --> 00:44:25.070
And it's really true.
而且确实如此。

1005
00:44:25.070 --> 00:44:35.730
I started rewatching these scenes, and we only used two cameras, but in each of the scenes, they set them up a little differently.
我开始重温这些场景，我们当时只用了两台摄像机，但在每个场景中，他们的机位设置都略有不同。

1006
00:44:35.730 --> 00:44:38.930
So you didn't feel like you were coming back to the same table.
所以你不会觉得你又回到了同一张桌子。

1007
00:44:39.070 --> 00:44:44.710
And as the scenes go on, the camera gets closer and closer and closer.
随着场景的推进，摄像机离得越来越近，越来越近。

1008
00:44:44.710 --> 00:44:49.450
So you really are like going into Michael's, like, little mind.
所以你真的就像是走进了迈克尔那小小的内心世界。

1009
00:44:49.750 --> 00:44:50.690
It's cool.
这很酷。

1010
00:44:50.890 --> 00:44:51.770
It's really cool.
真的很酷。

1011
00:44:51.770 --> 00:45:00.910
Well, we're going to go from this talk of being 49 nine years in a row, but actually being 58 with more sexy talk.
好了，我们要从谈论连续49年，但实际上已经58岁的话题，转到更多性感话题上了。

1012
00:45:01.390 --> 00:45:03.730
What name should she be called, Nana or Grandma?
她应该叫什么名字，娜娜还是奶奶？

1013
00:45:04.110 --> 00:45:04.710
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1014
00:45:04.850 --> 00:45:06.590
Michael's really feeling it now.
迈克尔现在真的很有感觉。

1015
00:45:06.850 --> 00:45:07.650
He is.
确实。

1016
00:45:07.930 --> 00:45:11.670
I noticed something at nine minutes and six seconds in this scene.
我注意到这个场景在9分06秒时有个细节。

1017
00:45:11.930 --> 00:45:12.170
What?
什么？

1018
00:45:12.570 --> 00:45:16.550
Do you notice how Steve eats his food as Michael Scott?
你注意到史蒂夫作为迈克尔·斯科特是怎么吃东西的吗？

1019
00:45:17.350 --> 00:45:20.110
It's exactly how he ate in Dinner Party.
这和他拍《晚宴》时吃东西的方式一模一样。

1020
00:45:20.110 --> 00:45:23.450
Well, he kind of scrapes the fork with his teeth.
嗯，他好像是用牙齿刮叉子上的食物。

1021
00:45:23.770 --> 00:45:24.210
Yes.
是的。

1022
00:45:24.410 --> 00:45:31.070
He eats tiny amounts of food off the tip of the fork with his very front teeth.
他用门牙从叉尖上吃极少量的食物。

1023
00:45:31.090 --> 00:45:33.970
He doesn't put the fork all the way in his mouth.
他不会把叉子整个放进嘴里。

1024
00:45:34.430 --> 00:45:37.250
He, like, bites it off the tip of the fork.
他就像是把食物从叉尖上咬下来一样。

1025
00:45:37.750 --> 00:45:38.710
It's very interesting.
这非常有意思。

1026
00:45:38.790 --> 00:45:40.530
He does not eat this way in real life.
他在现实生活中可不是这样吃东西的。

1027
00:45:40.530 --> 00:45:42.330
I've dined with him many times.
我和他一起吃过很多次饭。

1028
00:45:42.750 --> 00:45:46.070
This is clearly a Michael Scott eating choice.
这显然是迈克尔·斯科特式的进食选择。

1029
00:45:46.070 --> 00:45:53.370
It's either a Michael Scott eating choice or it's Steve the actor not wanting to eat the prop food and making the best of it.
这要么是迈克尔·斯科特的进食选择，要么是演员史蒂夫不想吃道具食物，所以尽量少吃点。

1030
00:45:53.450 --> 00:45:55.210
Because I would do something similar.
因为我也会做类似的事情。

1031
00:45:55.370 --> 00:46:01.510
I would just put the tiniest amount, like, on the end of the fork or spoon so I didn't have to eat too much of it.
我只会把极少量的食物放在叉子或勺子的尖端，这样我就不用吃太多了。

1032
00:46:01.510 --> 00:46:14.030
Well, now I guess I'd have to watch Steve's other films and see if he's eating in any of them and see if this is just his actor way of eating or if it was a character choice.
好吧，我想我得去看看史蒂夫的其他电影，看看他是否在里面吃东西，看看这只是他作为演员的进食习惯，还是角色的选择。

1033
00:46:14.210 --> 00:46:14.730
I'll investigate.
我会去调查一下。

1034
00:46:14.730 --> 00:46:21.650
I investigate, because with prop food, when you start out, it's usually really fresh and warm, and they've made it ready for you to eat.
我会调查的，因为道具食物刚开始时通常很新鲜、很热，他们已经为你准备好可以吃了。

1035
00:46:21.790 --> 00:46:28.810
But as each take goes, it gets colder and colder and a little bit more wilty, depending what you're eating.
但随着拍摄次数的增加，食物会变得越来越冷，根据你吃的东西不同，还会变得有点蔫。

1036
00:46:29.050 --> 00:46:32.650
And I just found early on the smaller bites are better.
我早早就发现，吃小口一点比较好。

1037
00:46:33.050 --> 00:46:33.210
True.
没错。

1038
00:46:33.810 --> 00:46:36.390
It's also lunchtime back at Dunder Mifflin.
邓德·米夫林那边也到了午餐时间。

1039
00:46:36.910 --> 00:46:41.890
And, oh my gosh, Andy has set up a whole taco buffet in the conference room.
天哪，安迪在会议室里摆了一整桌塔可自助餐。

1040
00:46:42.550 --> 00:46:45.370
Yes, but Dwight is going to volunteer to serve everyone.
是的，但德怀特主动提出要为大家服务。

1041
00:46:45.630 --> 00:46:45.890
Yes.
没错。

1042
00:46:46.250 --> 00:46:50.310
Did you notice at 9 minutes 26 seconds when Angela Martin enters?
你注意到9分26秒安吉拉·马丁进来的时候了吗？

1043
00:46:50.970 --> 00:46:51.490
Yes!
注意到了！

1044
00:46:51.650 --> 00:46:54.350
Her face she makes and she does a 180 out of the room?
她做的那个表情，然后直接转身离开了房间？

1045
00:46:54.550 --> 00:46:55.830
Well, because she's vegetarian.
嗯，因为她是素食主义者。

1046
00:46:56.210 --> 00:47:00.550
So I went to the script, because I was like, what did it say in the script about this moment?
所以我去查了剧本，因为我在想，剧本里关于这一刻是怎么写的？

1047
00:47:00.810 --> 00:47:05.130
In the script, it just says Angela Martin enters the room and immediately walks back out.
剧本里只写了安吉拉·马丁走进房间，然后立刻走了出去。

1048
00:47:05.790 --> 00:47:06.310
Oh!
噢！

1049
00:47:06.550 --> 00:47:11.650
So the face I made was just me, like, probably playing around in the moment.
所以我做的那个表情只是我当时即兴发挥的。

1050
00:47:11.890 --> 00:47:13.050
I have a question.
我有个问题。

1051
00:47:13.470 --> 00:47:15.850
Did you guys actually eat those tacos that day?
你们那天真的吃那些塔可了吗？

1052
00:47:16.010 --> 00:47:16.770
They looked good.
看起来很好吃。

1053
00:47:17.550 --> 00:47:20.330
We did not, just because it had to sit there for a bit.
我们没吃，因为它们得在那儿放一会儿。

1054
00:47:20.490 --> 00:47:20.850
Oh.
哦。

1055
00:47:21.010 --> 00:47:21.770
But we wanted to.
但我们本来想吃的。

1056
00:47:21.890 --> 00:47:23.750
When they first brought them out, we're like, woohoo, tacos!
当他们刚端上来的时候，我们就像，呜呼，塔可！

1057
00:47:23.910 --> 00:47:24.970
And we're like, no, no, no, guys.
然后我们又说，不，不，不，伙计们。

1058
00:47:25.450 --> 00:47:30.030
There's also a Kevin talking head and little moment that got deleted, probably for time.
还有一个凯文的单人采访镜头和一小段被删减了，可能是为了控制时长。

1059
00:47:30.170 --> 00:47:30.950
I loved it.
我很喜欢那段。

1060
00:47:31.630 --> 00:47:34.690
Kevin is so excited that Dwight is going to serve the tacos.
凯文因为德怀特要分发塔可而感到非常兴奋。

1061
00:47:35.370 --> 00:47:36.850
And he has this talking head.
然后他有这样一个单人采访。

1062
00:47:37.430 --> 00:47:38.350
This is great.
这太棒了。

1063
00:47:38.350 --> 00:47:39.350
I love tacos.
我爱吃塔可。

1064
00:47:39.590 --> 00:47:43.030
But whenever I try to make one, I get too excited and I crush it.
但每当我尝试做一个的时候，我总是太激动，结果把它捏碎了。

1065
00:47:43.310 --> 00:47:43.750
Oh!
哦！

1066
00:47:44.230 --> 00:47:48.090
And so then it cuts back to the scene and Dwight's making his taco.
然后镜头切回现场，德怀特正在做他的塔可。

1067
00:47:48.550 --> 00:47:49.750
Dwight hands it to Kevin.
德怀特把它递给凯文。

1068
00:47:49.950 --> 00:47:52.030
And Kevin's so excited, he crushes it in his hand.
凯文太兴奋了，他在手里把它捏碎了。

1069
00:47:52.150 --> 00:47:52.470
Oh!
哦！

1070
00:47:53.570 --> 00:47:54.010
Kevin!
凯文！

1071
00:47:55.690 --> 00:47:59.110
Well, after these guys compete to see who's going to serve the tacos,
好吧，在这些人比赛看谁来分发塔可之后，

1072
00:47:59.250 --> 00:48:01.810
now they're going to compete to see who's going to clean them up.
现在他们又要比赛看谁来负责清理。

1073
00:48:01.810 --> 00:48:03.050
It doesn't stop.
没完没了。

1074
00:48:03.190 --> 00:48:04.090
It doesn't stop.
没完没了。

1075
00:48:04.770 --> 00:48:07.710
Jenna, I'd like to break down all the gifts that Michael got Helene.
珍娜，我想盘点一下迈克尔送给海琳的所有礼物。

1076
00:48:08.230 --> 00:48:08.710
Oh!
哦！

1077
00:48:09.030 --> 00:48:11.330
And really show how all out he went for her.
并展示他为了她有多么用心。

1078
00:48:11.510 --> 00:48:13.010
Until he broke up with her.
直到他跟她分手为止。

1079
00:48:13.930 --> 00:48:15.130
He went all out.
他确实非常用心。

1080
00:48:15.410 --> 00:48:19.590
He got her the necklace and then also the lunch reservation, right?
他送了她项链，还有午餐预订，对吧？

1081
00:48:19.770 --> 00:48:20.010
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1082
00:48:20.290 --> 00:48:22.010
Where he decorated the table.
他还在那里装饰了餐桌。

1083
00:48:22.010 --> 00:48:24.450
I counted eight balloons, a birthday banner,
我数了数，有八个气球，一个生日横幅，

1084
00:48:24.650 --> 00:48:29.110
and also a really beautiful flower arrangement that none of the other tables had.
还有一个非常漂亮的花艺布置，其他桌子都没有。

1085
00:48:29.250 --> 00:48:29.550
Yes.
是的。

1086
00:48:29.770 --> 00:48:31.470
I assume she can take that with her.
我猜她可以把那个带走。

1087
00:48:31.470 --> 00:48:32.050
Yes.
是的。

1088
00:48:32.350 --> 00:48:34.570
As well as a scrapbook of their courtship.
还有一本记录他们恋爱过程的剪贴簿。

1089
00:48:34.790 --> 00:48:37.690
The wrapping paper says love in several different languages.
包装纸上用好几种语言写着“爱”。

1090
00:48:38.210 --> 00:48:41.310
Here are a few things that were in the scrapbook per the shooting draft.
根据拍摄剧本，剪贴簿里有以下几样东西。

1091
00:48:41.490 --> 00:48:43.470
Some made it in the episode, some did not.
有些出现在了剧集里，有些没有。

1092
00:48:43.690 --> 00:48:44.110
Oh!
哦！

1093
00:48:44.530 --> 00:48:47.730
The penny that Helene threw into the wishing well at the mall.
海琳在商场许愿池里投的那枚硬币。

1094
00:48:48.050 --> 00:48:49.330
Which doesn't exiSt.
那个许愿池根本不存在。

1095
00:48:49.910 --> 00:48:50.470
Right.
没错。

1096
00:48:51.090 --> 00:48:53.030
The fountain that doesn't exiSt.
那个不存在的喷泉。

1097
00:48:53.970 --> 00:48:58.790
Also, a ticket stub to a movie they went to together, Love Happens.
还有一张他们一起去看电影的票根，《爱上变身情人》。

1098
00:48:59.090 --> 00:48:59.550
Oh!
哦！

1099
00:48:59.770 --> 00:49:01.050
I looked up Love Happens.
我查了一下《爱上变身情人》。

1100
00:49:01.130 --> 00:49:05.230
It was a movie that was out in 2009 starring Jennifer Aniston and Aaron Eckhart.
那是2009年上映的一部电影，由詹妮弗·安妮斯顿和艾伦·艾克哈特主演。

1101
00:49:05.230 --> 00:49:10.750
As well as the poem that Michael wrote slash plagiarized from Shel Silverstein.
还有迈克尔写的那首诗，或者说是从谢尔·希尔弗斯坦那儿抄来的诗。

1102
00:49:11.370 --> 00:49:11.770
Hmm.
嗯。

1103
00:49:11.770 --> 00:49:13.090
Here was the poem.
诗是这样的。

1104
00:49:13.370 --> 00:49:16.790
I cannot go to school today, said little Peggy Ann McKay.
小佩吉·安·麦凯说，我今天不能去上学。

1105
00:49:16.950 --> 00:49:20.430
I have the measles and the mumps, a gash, a rash, and purple bumps.
我得了麻疹和腮腺炎，还有伤口、皮疹和紫色肿块。

1106
00:49:20.630 --> 00:49:22.150
My teacher's really mean.
我的老师真的很刻薄。

1107
00:49:22.410 --> 00:49:23.030
Happy birthday.
生日快乐。

1108
00:49:23.030 --> 00:49:24.250
I love you, Helene.
我爱你，海琳。

1109
00:49:24.910 --> 00:49:26.850
I mean, it's beautiful.
我是说，这写得很美。

1110
00:49:27.090 --> 00:49:28.330
It might be in my journal.
可能在我的日记里。

1111
00:49:30.530 --> 00:49:34.610
We had a fan question about the scrapbook from Carla B.
我们收到一个关于剪贴簿的粉丝提问，来自加利福尼亚州加迪纳的卡拉·B。

1112
00:49:34.850 --> 00:49:36.230
in Gardena, California.
在加利福尼亚州加迪纳。

1113
00:49:37.070 --> 00:49:43.610
The cover page of the scrapbook at the very bottom where it says, Love Copyright Michael.
剪贴簿封面的最底部写着，爱，版权所有，迈克尔。

1114
00:49:44.130 --> 00:49:47.390
We also see the letters XXLR.
我们还看到了字母XXLR。

1115
00:49:47.990 --> 00:49:50.110
Any idea what those letters stand for?
知道这些字母代表什么吗？

1116
00:49:51.010 --> 00:49:52.390
Do you know, Ange?
你知道吗，安吉？

1117
00:49:52.430 --> 00:49:52.810
I do.
我知道。

1118
00:49:53.030 --> 00:49:53.630
What is it?
是什么？

1119
00:49:53.670 --> 00:49:54.750
It's in the shooting draft.
拍摄剧本里有写。

1120
00:49:55.050 --> 00:49:55.730
Oh, tell us.
哦，告诉我们吧。

1121
00:49:55.770 --> 00:50:01.090
Because I thought they were Roman numerals, but when I looked it up, there's no R in Roman numerals.
因为我以为那是罗马数字，但我查了一下，罗马数字里没有R。

1122
00:50:01.210 --> 00:50:01.490
Yes.
没错。

1123
00:50:01.650 --> 00:50:06.270
So Helene reads that out loud, kind of like curious, and Michael goes, those are Roman numerals.
所以海琳好奇地大声读了出来，迈克尔就说，那是罗马数字。

